{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Klipy API","version":"1","description":"Klipy API lets you read and write core CRM records from Klipy, including people, companies, and interactions.\n\nAuthenticate every request with either `X-Klipy-Api-Key: <key>` or `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. API keys use the format `klipy_api_<id>`.\n\nEach endpoint requires a scope. Supported scopes are: `ALL`, `people:read`, `people:write`, `companies:read`, `companies:write`, `companies:remove`, `interactions:read`, and `interactions:write`.\n\nRate limiting is enforced per API key (200 requests per minute) and per organization (1000 requests per minute). Successful responses include `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `X-RateLimit-Reset`. When throttled, responses also include `Retry-After`.\n\nAll API responses use envelope objects that follow `{ object, data, meta }`. List responses also include `page_info`. Error responses use `{ object: \"error\", error, meta }`."},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.klipy.ai/api/v1","description":"Production"}],"tags":[{"name":"Authentication","description":"Endpoints for validating API key authentication."},{"name":"People","description":"Endpoints for reading and mutating person records."},{"name":"Companies","description":"Endpoints for reading and mutating company records."},{"name":"Interactions","description":"Endpoints for reading and creating interaction and activity records."}],"paths":{"/authenticate":{"get":{"tags":["Authentication"],"summary":"Authenticate API key","description":"Validates the provided API key and returns team information.","operationId":"authenticate","x-required-scope":"ALL","security":[{"ApiKeyHeader":[]},{"BearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Authentication succeeded","headers":{"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/XRateLimitLimit"},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/XRateLimitRemaining"},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/XRateLimitReset"}},"c